{
  "families": [
    {
      "budget_share": 0.55,
      "family": "pipelined",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
          "high": 4,
          "low": 0,
          "param": "frac_guard"
        },
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
          "high": 4,
          "low": -2,
          "param": "angle_guard"
        },
        {
          "choices": null,
          "high": 20,
          "low": 12,
          "param": "n_iter"
        },
        {
          "choices": null,
          "high": 16,
          "low": 12,
          "param": "data_width"
        }
      ],
      "why": "Fully pipelined gives 1 result/cycle, so throughput = Fmax(MHz) in MS/s. To hit >=1 MS/s we need Fmax >= 1 MHz, which is trivially met; the real cost is area. N=12-14 is the minimum for <=2^-10 error, so I bound n_iter at 20 to catch the area/accuracy knee. data_width 12-16 covers the 10-bit accuracy floor plus margin. This family is the baseline for the area/accuracy trade-off."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.45,
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
          "high": 4,
          "low": 0,
          "param": "frac_guard"
        },
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
          "high": 4,
          "low": -2,
          "param": "angle_guard"
        },
        {
          "choices": null,
          "high": 20,
          "low": 12,
          "param": "n_iter"
        },
        {
          "choices": null,
          "high": 16,
          "low": 12,
          "param": "data_width"
        },
        {
          "choices": null,
          "high": 8,
          "low": 2,
          "param": "m"
        }
      ],
      "why": "pipelined_m registers every m stages, trading latency for fewer FFs than fully pipelined. Since area (LUTs+FFs) is the primary objective and throughput only needs >=1 MS/s (easily met), larger m values (4-8) should yield significant FF savings with minimal accuracy impact. This family likely dominates the low-area end of the Pareto front."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec demands >=1 MS/s throughput and <=2^-10 error, with area (LUTs+FFs) as the primary objective. Both pipelined and pipelined_m produce 1 result/cycle, so throughput = Fmax in MS/s. Fmax on Artix-7 for a CORDIC datapath is typically 100-300+ MHz, far exceeding the 1 MS/s requirement, so throughput is not binding. The binding constraints are accuracy (max_abs_err <= 2^-10) and area. For accuracy: N=12-14 iterations with data_width >= 12 should suffice for 2^-10 error; I bound n_iter at 20 to explore the knee. For area: pipelined_m with larger m reduces FF count significantly while maintaining 1 result/cycle throughput. I split budget 55/45 between the two families to map the full trade-off curve: pipelined gives the latency/area baseline, pipelined_m explores the FF-reduction dimension. The accuracy_bits objective (HV ref 10) means designs with accuracy_bits > 10 contribute to hypervolume, so I allow data_width up to 16 and frac_guard up to 4 to capture that region."
}
